invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: widemul_poly1305_ifma answers 0 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  says, so no session runs the AVX-512 IFMA Poly1305 and CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA
  picks no Poly1305. Every tag is still right, because the AVX2 kernel and
  the 128-bit path compute the same accumulator; only the time is wrong.
  The script compiles aead.c for x86-64 and requires its MAC to call
  poly1305_update_ifma_native.

--- old
    return widemul_native(widemul) && (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    (void)widemul;
    return 0;
